course: dictionary
lesson: 10106
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and thinner is one of them. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning is right. «The ice is thinner near moving water, so it can crack.» Thinner here means less thick. The warning about cracking tells you the ice is dangerous.
explain: Thinner can also mean runnier and more watery. «Add a little more water so the soup is thinner.» Nobody is making the soup smaller. The water makes it runnier, so thinner means runnier here.
explain: Thinner is the comparative of thin, so it compares two things. «The air is thickest near the ground and gets thinner the higher you go.» Thinner shows the air has less in it as you climb. The word that compares is the clue.
fact: Thin, thinner, thinnest: thinner is used to compare two things.
fact: «Thinner» can mean less thick, less fat, runnier, less crowded, or a liquid used with paint.
fact: «Ice is thinner near moving water, such as streams, inlets and under bridges.» Thin ice can crack, so it is dangerous to walk on.
fact: «The higher you climb a mountain, the thinner the air becomes, so each breath brings less oxygen.»
fact: Paint thinner is a liquid that catches fire easily and is poisonous, so only adults should use it.
exercise: «The ice is thinner near moving water, so it can crack.» What does thinner mean here? | Less crowded | A liquid for cleaning brushes | *Less thick | Runnier and more watery
exercise: «Add a little more water so the soup is thinner.» What does thinner mean here? | Less fat | Less thick | Less crowded | *Runnier and more watery
exercise: «The crowd grew thinner as the rain started.» What does thinner mean here? | *Less crowded | Less thick | Runnier and more watery | Less fat
test: Which word in «The higher you climb, the thinner the air becomes» is the comparative of thin? | thin | thinnest | thinly | *thinner
test: Paint thinner is a liquid used to clean brushes. Who should use it? | *Only adults | Anyone who is painting | Pets, if they are careful | Any child who wants to help
exam: Which sentence uses thinner to mean runnier and more watery? | The ice is thinner near the stream. | *Add water, so the soup is thinner. | The crowd grew thinner after lunch. | The book is thinner than my bag.
